.Dd October 4, 2026
.Dt ITEFAN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm itefan
.Nd read and set fan speed on an ITE IT8613E Super I/O chip
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Cm show
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Cm set
.Ar channel duty
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Cm pct
.Ar channel percent
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Cm auto
.Ar channel
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility talks directly to the environment controller of the
ITE IT8613E Super I/O chip, as found in the UGREEN NASync DXP2800,
through
.Xr io 4 .
It can show the chip's temperature sensors, fan speeds and PWM settings,
and switch a fan channel between the chip's automatic mode and a fixed
speed.
.Pp
The chip has five PWM channels, numbered 1 to 5.
On the DXP2800 the system fan is on channel 3.
Unconnected channels report 0 rpm.
.Pp
A channel in
.Em manual
mode runs at the duty cycle last written to it, whatever the temperature.
A channel in
.Em auto
mode follows the fan curve programmed into the chip by the firmware.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width "pct channel percent"
.It Cm show
Show the chip ID, the environment controller address, the three
temperature sensors, and for each channel the fan speed in rpm,
the raw control register, the mode and the duty cycle.
This is the default when no command is given, and it changes nothing.
.It Cm set Ar channel duty
Put
.Ar channel
in manual mode at
.Ar duty ,
a raw value from 0 (off) to 255 (full speed).
.It Cm pct Ar channel percent
Same as
.Cm set ,
with the duty given as a percentage from 0 to 100.
A trailing
.Ql %
is accepted.
.It Cm auto Ar channel
Hand
.Ar channel
back to the chip's automatic mode.
.El
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-p port"
.It Fl f
Do not check the chip ID.
Without this option
.Nm
refuses to run on anything but an IT8613E, because other ITE chips
may use different registers.
.It Fl p Ar port
Use only the Super I/O configuration port
.Ar port ,
usually
.Li 0x2e
or
.Li 0x4e .
By default both are tried.
.El
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
The register layout follows the Linux it87 driver:
PWM control registers 0x15, 0x16, 0x17, 0x7f and 0xa7
.Pq bit 7 set means automatic ,
8-bit duty registers 0x63, 0x6b, 0x73, 0x7b and 0xa3,
and temperature registers 0x29 to 0x2b.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show the current state:
.Pp
.Dl # itefan
.Pp
Run the system fan at 40%:
.Pp
.Dl # itefan pct 3 40
.Pp
Give control back to the firmware:
.Pp
.Dl # itefan auto 3
.Pp
If the
.Xr fancurve 8
service is running, it overrides manual settings within one interval.
Stop it first:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# service fancurve stop
# itefan pct 3 40
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "itefan: open /dev/io (run as root): Permission denied"
Access to I/O ports needs root privileges.
.It "itefan: no ITE Super I/O found"
No ITE chip answered on the configuration ports.
.It "itefan: not an IT8613E; register map may differ"
A different ITE chip was found.
Use
.Fl f
only if its registers are known to match.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr io 4 ,
.Xr superio 4 ,
.Xr fancurve 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An pdillinger@gmail.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A fan left in manual mode at a low duty cycle will not speed up when the
system gets hot.
Use
.Cm auto
or
.Xr fancurve 8
for unattended operation.
.Pp
.Nm
accesses the hardware without locking.
Do not run it while another program or kernel driver, such as
.Xr superio 4
with a hardware monitor attached, is using the same chip.
.Pp
The firmware may reprogram the chip at boot or after suspend.
